| The workspace's colours, in one file, linked by every application.
|
| Seven roles and nothing else, from the design: the page and any band that
| should recede; every panel, at one elevation and never nested; one pixel
| of border doing all the separating; text being read; text supporting it;
| one accent, spent on at most one filled button per view plus link text;
| and green for a service's health, which only an administrator sees.
|
| **This file is linked, not copied.** The shell and its guests share one
| origin and one theme, so a colour that differs between them is a bug —
| and before this existed there were a hundred and thirty-nine hard-coded
| hex values across seven applications, with five of them ignoring the
| theme switch outright.
|
| The theme is the shell's choice, kept in the origin's storage under
| `ui:theme`. Every application reads it; none offers a switch. An
| application links this and asks `Palette` whenever it draws.

| Light and dark are not the same palette with the lightness flipped: the
| page and the panel **swap roles**. A panel is lighter than the page in
| the dark theme and darker in the light one, which is what keeps a panel
| reading as a panel rather than as a hole.
Palette =>
    emit Get { key = "ui:theme" } to store get chosen
    if chosen.value = "light"
        return Colours {
            bg = "#ffffff"
            panel = "#f6f8fa"
            line = "#d0d7de"
            fg = "#1f2328"
            muted = "#656d76"
            accent = "#0969da"
            health = "#1a7f37"
            health_soft = "#dafbe1"
            danger = "#cf222e"
            danger_soft = "#ffebe9"
            warn = "#9a6700"
            warn_soft = "#fff8c5"
            accent_soft = "#ddf4ff"
            header = "rgba(255,255,255,0.97)"
            hover = "#eaeef2"
        }
    return Colours {
        bg = "#0d1117"
        panel = "#161b22"
        line = "#30363d"
        fg = "#e6edf3"
        muted = "#9da7b3"
        accent = "#2f81f7"
        health = "#3fb950"
        health_soft = "#172d20"
        danger = "#f85149"
        danger_soft = "#321b20"
        | Amber, for a service that is degraded rather than down. Only
        | System Monitor has ever needed it.
        warn = "#d29922"
        warn_soft = "#2d2607"
        accent_soft = "#17243a"
        header = "rgba(22,27,34,0.97)"
        hover = "#1f242d"
    }

| Type and shape, so two applications do not disagree about what a button
| is. Sizes that differ between a phone and a desktop are one `clamp`:
| a stylesheet here is a selector to a flat set of properties, so there
| are no media queries to be had.
Metrics =>
    return Sizes {
        sans = "system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif"
        mono = "ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace"
        | The hub's headline, and the only display type in the workspace.
        display = "clamp(30px, 6vw, 52px)"
        lead = "clamp(15px, 1.4vw, 17px)"
        app_large = "clamp(19px, 2.2vw, 24px)"
        app_small = "15px"
        heading = "clamp(19px, 2.2vw, 24px)"
        body = "clamp(14px, 1.2vw, 15px)"
        meta = "12.5px"
        label = "11px"
        | Never smaller: a button is pressed with a thumb. And never under
        | 16px for an input, or Safari zooms the page on focus.
        button = "15px"
        field = "16px"
        gutter = "clamp(20px, 4vw, 40px)"
        | Content capped so a wide screen does not stretch a line of text
        | past reading width.
        page = "1120px"
        radius = "12px"
        control = "10px"
        tap = "46px"
    }

| Task priority — the one place colour carries meaning rather than mood.
| It reads as a stripe down the left edge of a task, so these are the four
| steps of a scale and are deliberately not the accent, which is spent on
| buttons and links. Here rather than in To Do because a second
| application showing a priority must show the same four.
Priorities =>
    emit Palette to this get c
    return Steps {
        urgent = c.danger
        high = "#db6d28"
        medium = c.warn
        low = c.health
    }
